1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,970
Playing Games

2
00:00:04,970 --> 00:00:06,220
Oh, Daddy!

3
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:08,170
We had such a good time at the aquarium.

4
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:09,260
I saw a real shark.

5
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:10,550
I could almost touch it.

6
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:12,420
I'm so glad.

7
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:13,740
Hi. Michelle,

8
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:15,610
why don't you introduce everybody to Susan?

9
00:00:15,610 --> 00:00:16,220
Hi, Susan.

10
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:17,490
Hi.

11
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:20,670
I'd like you to meet Audrey and her mother, Mrs. Cooper.

12
00:00:20,670 --> 00:00:21,590
Hello, Audrey.

13
00:00:21,590 --> 00:00:22,910
Nice to meet you, Mrs. Cooper.

14
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:24,430
I'm Susan Stewart.

15
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:26,910
And this is Shirley and Nicole.

16
00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:28,550
Hi, girls.

17
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:29,060
Come on in.

18
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:29,890
Come on in, Mrs. Cooper.

19
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:30,820
Come on in, everybody.

20
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:32,050
The aquarium was so exciting.

21
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:33,700
I had never been there before.

22
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,540
The girls learned a great deal.

23
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:35,970
Frankly, so did I.

24
00:00:35,970 --> 00:00:38,340
Well, please sit down

25
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:40,080
and tell us all about it during lunch.

26
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:42,070
We prepared some tuna fish

27
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:44,800
and cheese sandwiches for lunch.

28
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,290
I love tuna fish.

29
00:00:46,290 --> 00:00:50,200
Don't you, Audrey?

30
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:52,570
I remember when I used to be a Girl Scout.

31
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:55,900
My mother would take us everywhere, too.

32
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:58,090
Susan, I understand you're in the toy business.

33
00:00:58,090 --> 00:00:59,100
Yes, I am.

34
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,060
My company manufactures toys and games for children.

35
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:04,550
Susan's vice-president in charge of new toys and games.

36
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:06,800
And the marketing of new toys and games.

37
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,980
Can we test a new game for you, Susan?

38
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:10,530
That's an excellent idea, Michelle.

39
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:12,430
I happen to have

40
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:13,260
a game which I brought home to study.

41
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:14,060
Let us try it!

42
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:15,630
Do you want to play?

43
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:19,790
Nicole? Shirley? Audrey?

44
00:01:19,790 --> 00:01:23,010
We tested it last week on twelve- to fifteen-year-olds,

45
00:01:23,010 --> 00:01:25,860
and they found it to be too easy--

46
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:27,710
in other words ... boring.

47
00:01:27,710 --> 00:01:30,830
We think it might be just right for ten- to twelve-year-olds.

48
00:01:30,830 --> 00:01:31,950
That's us, Susan.

49
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:35,660
First, you shuffle the deck

50
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:39,670
and lay them face down.

51
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:41,940
Then you select the leader.

52
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:44,280
I'll be the leader.

53
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:47,220
The leader takes the first ten cards

54
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:50,380
and lays them face up on this stand.

55
00:01:50,380 --> 00:02:12,600
h-t-e-r-c-z-e-p-e-s.

56
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:15,290
Everyone gets a turn, going counterclockwise,

57
00:02:15,290 --> 00:02:17,060
left to right.

58
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:23,020
You have thirty seconds to make a word,

59
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:25,650
using as many letters as possible.

60
00:02:25,650 --> 00:02:28,300
You get one point for each letter,

61
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:33,390
plus the person with the longest word gets ten extra points.

62
00:02:33,390 --> 00:02:36,350
The first one to get one hundred points wins.

63
00:02:36,350 --> 00:02:37,670
That's easy.

64
00:02:37,670 --> 00:02:40,350
OK, let's go around the table.

65
00:02:40,350 --> 00:02:49,370
You first, Audrey.

66
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:56,500
Chest--c-h-e-s-t.

67
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:57,750
Good.

68
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:00,130
That's five points.

69
00:03:00,130 --> 00:03:07,400
Next, Nicole.

70
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:14,700
Three--t-h-r-e-e.

71
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:15,550
OK.

72
00:03:15,550 --> 00:03:17,710
That's five points also.

73
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:25,600
It's your turn, Shirley.

74
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:32,980
Creep--c-r-e-e-p.

75
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:34,270
Creep.

76
00:03:34,270 --> 00:03:36,170
That's another five-letter word.

77
00:03:36,170 --> 00:03:36,990
Five points.

78
00:03:36,990 --> 00:03:38,920
So far, you're all tied.

79
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,760
Sheet--s-h-e-e-t.

80
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:46,000
Sheet is a five-letter word.

81
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,480
Michelle, your turn.

82
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:51,870
Cheese--c-h-e-e-s-e.

83
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:52,520
Terrific!

84
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,390
Michelle wins with a six-letter word,

85
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:57,370
plus she gets an additional ten points

86
00:03:57,370 --> 00:03:59,270
for a total of sixteen points.

87
00:03:59,270 --> 00:04:01,060
How are you enjoying the game so far?

88
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:03,360
I think it's too easy.

89
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:05,190
Too easy?

90
00:04:05,190 --> 00:04:06,310
Michelle!

91
00:04:06,310 --> 00:04:07,340
It's OK, Harry.

92
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:08,900
Michelle is quite right.

93
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:10,970
She just said it's too easy.

94
00:04:10,970 --> 00:04:13,640
Well, I like the game.

95
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,150
I enjoyed lunch, Susan.

96
00:04:15,150 --> 00:04:16,320
Thank you so much,

97
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:17,650
but we have to get going

98
00:04:17,650 --> 00:04:20,210
to meet the rest of the troop at two o'clock at the museum.

99
00:04:20,210 --> 00:04:23,040
Oh, it was nice meeting all of you.

100
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,620
I hope you have a wonderful time

101
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:26,450
at the Museum of Natural History.

102
00:04:26,450 --> 00:04:27,470
Good-bye, everybody.

103
00:04:27,470 --> 00:04:28,080
Have a good time.

104
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:29,030
Bye.

105
00:04:29,030 --> 00:04:29,830
See you in front of the museum at five o'clock.

106
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:32,220
Oh, OK.

107
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:32,660
Thanks, Mr. Bennett.

108
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:33,780
That'll be fine.

109
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:37,480
And thanks again for the lunch and for the game.

110
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:39,320
Good-bye, Susan.

111
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,760
It's not a bad game.

112
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:43,970
It's just ... slow.

113
00:04:43,970 --> 00:04:46,490
Just slow.

114
00:04:46,490 --> 00:04:48,940
You helped save our company a lot of money.

115
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:59,650
Bye-bye.

116
00:04:59,650 --> 00:05:03,810
You are wonderful with kids.

117
00:05:03,810 --> 00:05:05,880
I am.

118
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:08,880
Isn't there a conversation that we have to finish?
